.TH MIKROTIK-HOME-NETFLOW-PLUS 8 "October 2026" "mikrotik-home-netflow-plus" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mikrotik-home-netflow-plus \- network traffic per connection and per device for MikroTik routers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mikrotik-home-netflow-plus
.br
.B mikrotik-home-netflow-plus version
.br
.B mikrotik-home-netflow-plus healthcheck
.br
.B mikrotik-home-netflow-plus replay
.I capture.bin
.RI [ host:port
.RI [ speed ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mikrotik-home-netflow-plus
receives IPFIX flow records exported by a MikroTik router (RouterOS Traffic
Flow) on UDP port 2055, optionally polls the RouterOS API with a read-only
user for second-by-second rates and device names, and serves a web
interface on TCP port 8080 showing traffic per connection and per device,
right now and over the last days, with alerts and a full-screen wall
display at
.IR /dashboard .
.PP
The Debian package runs it as the systemd service
.BR mikrotik-home-netflow-plus.service ,
as the system user of the same name, with its database under
.IR /var/lib/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus .
Settings are read from
.IR /etc/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus/env ;
restart the service after editing it.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B healthcheck
Exit 0 if the web interface answers on the configured listen address, 1
otherwise. Used by the container image's health check.
.TP
.BI replay " capture.bin " [ host:port " [" speed ]]
Send a recorded flow export capture to a collector (default 127.0.0.1:2055)
with its original timing, optionally sped up. A development aid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every setting is an environment variable; the service reads them from
.IR /etc/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus/env .
Secrets can also be given as a file name in
.IB NAME _FILE\fR.
The full reference, with the reasoning behind each default, is in the README
listed under FILES.
.TP
.B NFP_EXPORTERS
Addresses allowed to send flow records, comma separated. Default: the
router API host; with neither set, records from any address are accepted.
.TP
.BR NFP_ROUTER_ADDR ", " NFP_ROUTER_USER ", " NFP_ROUTER_PASSWORD
Router API host and the read-only user (policy
.BR read,api ).
Without NFP_ROUTER_ADDR the collector runs from flow records only.
.TP
.B NFP_ROUTER_TLS
.B true
for api-ssl on port 8729 (the certificate is pinned on first use),
.B false
for the plain API on 8728. Default: true.
.TP
.B NFP_ROUTER_CERT_FINGERPRINT
Expected SHA-256 fingerprint of the router's API certificate, instead of
trust on first use.
.TP
.BR NFP_LOCAL_NETS ", " NFP_SITES ", " NFP_WAN_INTERFACES
Override the networks discovered from the router: local prefixes, named
remote sites as
.IR name=cidr ,
and WAN interface names.
.TP
.BR NFP_HTTP_LISTEN ", " NFP_FLOW_LISTEN
Listen addresses. Defaults: :8080 and :2055.
.TP
.B NFP_AUTH_PASSWORD
Require this password for the web interface. Default: no login.
.TP
.BR NFP_RETENTION_CONNECTIONS ", " NFP_RETENTION_1M ", " NFP_RETENTION_1H
How long to keep the connection log, per-minute and per-hour history.
Defaults: 48h, 7d, 30d.
.TP
.BR NFP_FOLD_BELOW ", " NFP_DB_MAX_SIZE
Connections smaller than NFP_FOLD_BELOW (default 10KB) are folded into a
per-device summary; the database is pruned to stay under NFP_DB_MAX_SIZE
(default 2GB).
.TP
.B NFP_FLUSH_INTERVAL
How often accumulated data is written to the database, 1s to 10m. Default
20s; 60s is recommended on SD cards.
.TP
.B NFP_ACTIVE_FLOW_TIMEOUT
The router's active-flow-timeout. Default 1m.
.TP
.B NFP_ASN_DB
Path to a MaxMind-format IP to ASN database. Default: asn.mmdb in the data
directory, as written by
.BR mikrotik-home-netflow-plus-fetch-asn (8).
.TP
.BR NFP_DATA_DIR ", " NFP_LOG_LEVEL
Data directory (the service sets /var/lib/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus) and
log level (debug, info, warn, error; default info).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus/env
Settings, readable by root only.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus/
Database, flow template cache, pinned router certificate and the optional
organisation database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus/
README.md, SETUP-MIKROTIK-ROUTER.md and an example RouterOS script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mikrotik-home-netflow-plus-fetch-asn (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/thedyerman/mikrotik-home-netflow-plus
